                    href=\"/the-simpsons/matt-groening\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Created By\"\n                >\n                    <strong>Matt Groening</strong>\n                    <span>Matthew Abram &quot;Matt&quot; Groening (pronounced GREY-ning) is the creator of the comic strip Life in Hell and television series The Simpsons, Futurama and Disenchantment. Groening made his first professional cartoon sale of…</span>\n                </a>\n            \n        </div>\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Created By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/the-simpsons/matt-groening\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Matt Groening\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Matt Groening created The Simpsons.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>The Simpsons is also referenced as Simpsons, The Simpsons TV show.</li><li>The TV series is the core of The Simpsons.</li><li>Matt Groening created The Simpsons.</li><li>The movie is part of The Simpsons franchise.</li><li>Part of</li><li>Evidence around The Simpsons is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is The Simpsons?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        The Simpsons (often shortened to Simpsons) is an American long-running animated sitcom created by <a href=\"/the-simpsons/matt-groening\" class=\"entity-link\">Matt Groening</a> for the Fox Broadcasting Company. The main characters are a satire of a working-class family, consisting of Homer, Marge, Bart, Lisa, and Maggie. The series lampoons many aspects of American culture, society, politics, and history.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The cartoon made its debut as 60-second animated bumpers for The Tracey Ullman Show, with the first short airing on April 19, 1987. The shorts were then expanded into a full-length 30-minute television spin-off by Gracie Films and 20th Century Fox, first airing on December 17, 1989. As of 2025, 36 seasons have aired, and the 36th season ended on May 18, 2025, and Season 37 is currently airing as of September 28, 2025.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The series currently holds the record for the longest-running prime-time sitcom in the US, running for 35 years and 36 seasons, as well as three seasons of shorts since 1989, and has become the longest-running program on FOX.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The Simpsons was conceived in the lobby of James L. Brooks&#039;s office by <a href=\"/the-simpsons/matt-groening\" class=\"entity-link\">Matt Groening</a>. He was asked to do a series of animated shorts, and decided to do his Life in Hell series; since he realized that animating Life in Hell would require the rescinding of publication rights for his life&#039;s work, he chose another approach and formulated his version of a dysfunctional family. He named the characters after his own family and substituted Bart for his own name, as it was an anagram of &#039;brat&#039;.\n    </p>\n    \n    <p class=\"also-known-as\">\n        <strong>Also known as:</strong>\n        Simpsons, The Simpsons TV show.\n    </p>\n\n</section>","word_count":971,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"65f5084d-c0b6-4463-9b90-9b97990344ba","name":"The Simpsons","slug":"the-simpsons","type":"topic","kind":"topic","type_label":"Topic","short_description":"The Simpsons (often shortened to Simpsons) is an American long-running animated sitcom created by Matt Groening for the Fox Broadcasting Company. The main characters are a satire of a working-class family, consisting of…","description":"The Simpsons (often shortened to Simpsons) is an American long-running animated sitcom created by Matt Groening for the Fox Broadcasting Company. The main characters are a satire of a working-class family, consisting of Homer, Marge, Bart, Lisa, and Maggie. The series lampoons many aspects of American culture, society, politics, and history.\n\nThe cartoon made its debut as 60-second animated bumpers for The Tracey Ullman Show, with the first short airing on April 19, 1987. The shorts were then expanded into a full-length 30-minute television spin-off by Gracie Films and 20th Century Fox, first airing on December 17, 1989. As of 2025, 36 seasons have aired, and the 36th season ended on May 18, 2025, and Season 37 is currently airing as of September 28, 2025.\n\nThe series currently holds the record for the longest-running prime-time sitcom in the US, running for 35 years and 36 seasons, as well as three seasons of shorts since 1989, and has become the longest-running program on FOX.\n\nThe Simpsons was conceived in the lobby of James L. Brooks's office by Matt Groening. He was asked to do a series of animated shorts, and decided to do his Life in Hell series; since he realized that animating Life in Hell would require the rescinding of publication rights for his life's work, he chose another approach and formulated his version of a dysfunctional family. He named the characters after his own family and substituted Bart for his own name, as it was an anagram of 'brat'.","evidence":"fiction","universe":"the-simpsons","aliases":["Simpsons","The Simpsons TV show"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"connections":[],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"the-simpsons","title":"The Simpsons is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"The Simpsons, its characters, artwork, logos, and related intellectual property are the property of their respective rights holders, including Matt Groening, 20th Century Studios, Fox Broadcasting Company, and The Walt Disney Company and other credited rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders. Identification logos and thumbnails, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"the-simpsons","name":"The Simpsons","theme":"the-simpsons","path":"/the-simpsons","logo":{"license":"fair_use","usage":"fair_use_identification","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/The_Simpsons_yellow_logo.svg/330px-The_Simpsons_yellow_logo.svg.png","alt":"The Simpsons logo","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Simpsons_yellow_logo.svg","credit":"Fair-use identification logo via Wikimedia Commons. © Matt Groening / 20th Television / Disney."},"categories":["television"]}}